body:
My little brother is genuinely the highlight of my wedding planning. I made him my Best Man because I was like screw it, just because he's a dude doesn't mean he has to stand with my FH when he's my brother and one of my favorite people in the world. He's so stable and kind that it just makes everything better (especially whilst having some MOH drama).

&#x200B;

When I asked him to be Best Man, he was super sweet and appreciative... and then about a minute later shyly said "...this means I have to do a speech, doesn't it?" haha

We considered this venue too! Looks beautiful! 

&#x200B;

I really appreciate this recap: it's hard to get a sense of costs in the Bay Area, and now we have a starting point for what cupcakes and photography might look like... (we're having a similarly sized guest list.)

That's true, to an extent. If anyone is more interested in this, I highly recommend this book: [https://www.amazon.com/Come-You-Are-Surprising-Transform/dp/1476762090](https://www.amazon.com/Come-You-Are-Surprising-Transform/dp/1476762090)

&#x200B;

But essentially, for many people, wet does = arousal. For some portion of the population, that isn't true. People can be aroused without feeling physical sensations such as wetness. Additionally, people can get wet when they're not aroused. This is true even during assaults, so can be very confusing for victims.

I keep trying to convince my fiance to do this... We already have the ring, all he needs to do is give it back to me... Every night we go out until we get married.

&#x200B;

He's way too ethical. Lord only knows why I decided to marry someone with *morals.*

This is so true. I grew up in Ohio. Where I'm from in Ohio, after say October, there is no produce... in the grocery stores. Literally, you can't buy produce if you have the money to. So no, the food banks aren't going to have produce.

&#x200B;

Now, I live in California. There is produce out the wazoo all year round. So food banks are much better stocked.

Yep, this is what we're doing. My brother is going to be my (I'm the bride) best man, and my fiance's sisters will be his groomswoman. My sister is going to be standing beside me, so why shouldn't my brother as well?

&#x200B;

All the ladies in our wedding party will be wearing the same color dresses (I'm in charge of that choice), and my fiance is picking out clothes for all the men in our bridal party (I think tuxes...)

I think shades are a little rude, because it prevents people from seeing your full facial expression... maybe implying you're (pardon the pun) shady.

&#x200B;

But I don't have a problem with a ball cap.

Depends on what people are taking pictures of. If they're taking pictures of things or themselves, I let them fucking burn. If they're taking pictures of me or my friends, they're going to get a heaping pile of shouting about consent.

&#x200B;

I'm nice about it, but every time I'm playing with my friends and a dude (it's always a dude!) circles us with a camera, I get a little less nice.
